+### Scores and prizes
+
+In **Settings**, set **Number of winners** (at least 1, default 3). Each new game
+snapshots this setting alongside the questions. Each correct final answer earns
+one point. Equal scores are ranked by the total server-measured time of correct
+answers, from question opening to the last pick. Points stay hidden during play.
+
+After **End quiz**, the big screen shows every player's place, name, and points;
+phones show their own place and points. Use **Top N** (for example, **Top 3**) to
+award prizes in leaderboard order. **Draw** guarantees prizes to players above
+the cutoff score, then draws the remaining prizes among everyone tied on that
+score, ignoring speed. Each click draws afresh and may repeat the same result.
+Players with zero points never win; if fewer than N have points, all of them win.
+**Reset winners** removes all awards. **Winner** marks and **You won!** on phones
+update live, including after reloads and reconnections.
+
+SQLite persists games, players, final choices, timings, and awards across restarts. Live presence
 uses connection tracking and short heartbeat leases for unreliable Wi-Fi; saved
 answers remain even if a player disconnects. The stage's answer counter is saved
 answers / currently connected players. All assets, QR generation, and live
