 - Rust tests additionally exercise public projections, lease expiration,
   multi-tab presence, and cascading cleanup. Existing CRUD/import/export/preview
   browser and HTTP suites continue to pass.
+
+
+## Scores and prizes
+
+- `quizzes.number_of_winners` is an integer, default 3, with HTML, server, and
+  SQLite validation (minimum 1). Games snapshot it at creation. Settings edits
+  therefore affect future games, not already-running games. The portable JSON
+  accepts `number_of_winners`, defaults missing values to 3, and emits it when
+  non-default, preserving the original default export shape.
+- Opening a question stores `games.opened_at_us` on the server in the same
+  transaction as its phase/version change. Accepted answer upserts replace both
+  the choice and `answers.elapsed_us`. Time is server receipt time minus opening
+  time, in microseconds, not a client-supplied duration. Clock and answer durations
+  survive restarts; negative wall-clock differences are clamped to zero. The
+  server clock should be kept stable during a conference. Client clocks cannot
+  influence ranking. Delivery cannot be literally simultaneous across a network,
+  but SSE invalidations have no polling/batching delay (local browser tests
+  observed 5–29 ms spread across six screens).
+- Every phone tap has a random `pick_token`; retries retain it. Repeated receipt
+  of the current token does not change its choice or duration. A new tap, even
+  on the same option, has a new token and replaces the duration. Existing clients
+  without a token remain supported and each request counts as a pick. No server
+  correctness, points, ranking, or timing data is exposed to phones during play.
+- `src/prizes.rs` derives points from each game's immutable question snapshot and
+  final answers. Only correct answers contribute a point and elapsed time. The
+  leaderboard includes *all registered players*, not only currently connected
+  phones. Sort order: descending points, ascending sum of correct-answer times,
+  then ascending player ID for a deterministic order on exact time ties. Places
+  are unique, 1-based. Wrong answers and missing answers contribute neither time
+  nor points. No stored/cached score can drift from the answers.
+- Top N filters zero scores and takes the first N. Draw finds the Nth eligible
+  score (or the last eligible score when fewer exist), guarantees players above
+  it, and shuffles the tied pool with unbiased Fisher–Yates using local OS
+  randomness. Speed is irrelevant to the draw. Each draw replaces the previous
+  set; a repeated result is valid. Empty/all-zero games have no winners.
+- Winner flags live on game-scoped players. Authenticated, CSRF-protected,
+  version-checked actions are permitted only after the game ends. Reset, new
+  flags, and version/revision changes commit atomically. There are no client-side
+  decisions or external draw services.
+- Ended SSE streams stay open on both server and browser, and ended pages also
+  subscribe when reloaded. Winner updates use the same full-state projection and
+  revision guard as gameplay. Only the moderator gets the complete leaderboard;
+  a phone receives only its own final place/points/winner flag and player count.
+- Additive, idempotent migrations upgrade existing databases without deleting
+  quizzes or game records. Historic answers made before timing existed receive
+  elapsed time 0 (their true speed cannot be reconstructed). A legacy question
+  still open at upgrade starts its clock once at upgrade; subsequent restarts
+  never reset it. New games have fully measured timing from their first question.
+
+### Prize verification
+
+- `tests/prizes.py`: reproduces the original missing-setting failure; covers
+  validation, persisted/snapshotted prize count, last-pick ranking, points,
+  registered zero-point/missing-answer players, rerolls, top/reset/auth, fewer
+  eligible players than prizes, empty games, and all-zero games.
+- `tests/prizes_browser.py`: actual isolated Chromium contexts for four phones
+  and two moderators; form defaults/validation, measured delivery spread, no
+  points during play, exact labels and separate leaderboard list items, live
+  top/draw/reset from either moderator tab, reconnecting an ended phone, no
+  reloads, and desktop/mobile layout checks/screenshots.
+- `tests/live_game_persistence.py` now verifies stored opening clock, final-answer
+  duration, rankings, winners, reset, and graceful shutdown with an ended stream
+  held open, across offline launcher restarts.
+- Rust unit tests cover total correct-answer time (not fastest/first answer),
+  ignoring wrong-answer time, final-pick timing and idempotent retries, empty and
+  sparse winner pools, reroll tie boundaries and no duplicate/zero-point winners.
